      "content": "That makes sense. You mentioned the tenant needs to prove the event was \"unforeseeable and unavoidable.\" In these kinds of disputes, does the court look for evidence of some kind of external, chaotic disruption that is essentially impossible for a normal business to prepare for, or do they stick strictly to the literal definitions of the terms provided in the lease?",
